* Is note encryption\nconstrained on Aztec?
** The question
*** AES is byte-oriented,\na poor circuit fit
*** Aztec pushes much\nto unconstrained oracles
*** So doubt is reasonable
** Three delivery modes
*** offchain()\nno data, no proof
*** onchain_unconstrained()\nlog, no proof
*** onchain_constrained()\nlog + proof
** The answer
*** Docs: encryption AND tag\nare constrained
*** Cost line says\n"proving time for encryption"
*** std::aes128::aes128_encrypt\nis the Noir stdlib
*** Decryption is an oracle\ntry_aes128_decrypt
** Where the constraints live
*** The contract's circuit,\nnot the kernels
*** profile gates attributes\nthem per function
*** AES-128 absent\nfrom the AVM
** Cost and design
*** ~20,200 gates\nper delivery, measured
*** Paid in the user's\nproving time
*** Choice is per recipient,\nnot per contract
*** Caps batch sizes
** Found in the source
*** Invalid address encrypts\nto a random one
*** Prevents king-of-the-hill
*** Padding is unconstrained\nrandom, deliberately
*** Test: who is hurt\nif it is wrong?
@endmindmap
